229.Majority Element II.cpp


###  Intuition
<!-- Explain your thought process and initial approach to the problem -->
The problem requires finding all elements that appear more than ⌊n/3⌋ times in an array.
Since there can be at most two such elements, I decided to count the frequency of each element and collect those that satisfy this condition.



### Approach
<!-- Describe your solution approach in detail -->

- Used an unordered_map to count the frequency of every element in the array.

- Iterated through the map to check which elements have a count greater than ⌊n/3⌋.

- Stored those elements in a result vector and returned it.

- The approach runs in O(n) time and uses O(n) extra space.



## Code Solution (C++)

```cpp
    // Your code goes here
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> majorityElement(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<int> ans;
        unordered_map<int,int> mpp;

        for (auto it : nums) {
            mpp[it]++;
        }

        for (auto it : mpp) {
            if (it.second > n / 3) {
                ans.push_back(it.first);
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};


    
``` 


